## **4.1 Special methodological considerations for recommendations on prophylactic interventons**

## **Implicatons of very low event rates**

Prophylactc interventons are administered to prevent the occurrence of an illness among individuals who are not yet sick. A minority will develop the illness and, of those, a minority will develop complicatons from the illness. Accordingly, the number of critcally important events (e.g. death) in studies evaluatng prophylactc interventons is typically very low. For that reason, researchers may choose to measure the efectveness of prophylactc interventons by measuring their impact on outcomes that are more common albeit less critcally important for patents, such as the development of the illness.

